WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:03.870
- [Narrator] This small
islet in Spain is connected

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.093
to the mainland by a narrow man-made path.

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:10.000
And fans of Game of
Thrones might recognize it

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.225
as the ancestral home to
the Mother of Dragons.

00:00:13.225 --> 00:00:15.975
(peaceful music)

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:24.550
Gaztelugatxe can be found
in Basque Country in Spain

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.100
and is home to a small chapel

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.383
that is dedicated to John the Baptist.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.940
The narrow stone bridge
that connects the islet

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:37.940
consists of 231 zig-zagging
steps leading up to the chapel.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.700
Legend has it that if
visitors make it to the top

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.000
and ring the bell on the
exterior three times,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.393
a wish will be granted.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:46.970
A structure was first built

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:48.840
on the island in the ninth century.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.600
However, since then it has
been destroyed, rebuilt,

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:54.060
and changed purposes many times.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.170
Its uses have ranged from a convent

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:58.480
to serving as a site of imprisonment

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:01.303
for accused witches during
the Spanish Inquisition.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.570
In season seven of Game of Thrones,

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:08.090
Gaztelugatxe made an
appearance as Dragonstone,

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:11.060
causing its popularity to skyrocket.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:14.250
Thousands of visitors flock
to this recognizable location

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:17.670
for its beauty or perhaps
simply in hopes of one day

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:20.513
catching themselves a glimpse
of Daenerys Targaryen.

00:01:21.486 --> 00:01:24.319
(peaceful music)

